ed to prove itself valuable in following operations, including the Battle of Kursk in 1943, where it contributed to the Soviet victory in the largest tank battles in history. Later, the 16th Guards Tank Division participated in major Soviet offensives, such as Operation Bagration in 1944, helping push German forces back through Belarus and eventually to Eastern Europe. By the end of the war, the division had advanced into Germany where it participated in the Battle of Berlin, which led to the final defeat of Nazi Germany. After the war the division was stationed in Eastern Germany until 1991 when the Soviet Union was dissolved, resulting in the withdrawal of remaining units from Germany."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Fight"],"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/Winter_2024/t_57th_rifles.t_57th_rifles","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Soviet WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/57th_RIFLES.57th_RIFLES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":345.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_57th_rifles_photo","SourceString":"Soviet Infantry and tank during the Battle of Berlin, April 24th, 1945.","LocalizedString":"Soviet Infantry and tank during the Battle of Berlin, April 24th, 1945."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryM.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"isDefenseBuff":true,"threa